 <section class="instrument"><div class="instrument-head"><span>YOUR LIVING INSTRUMENT</span><span id="scene-label">VELVET MIST</span></div><div class="body"><div class="screen-wrap"><canvas id="screen" class="screen" width="240" height="240" aria-label="Live 240 by 240 pixel firmware display"></canvas><div class="screen-label">MUTABLE DREAMS DISPLAY · 240 × 240</div></div><div><nav class="pages" id="pages"></nav><div class="macro-grid" id="macros"></div><div class="performance"><button data-hw="1" id="mute">SEL · Mute track</button><button data-hw="8" id="lock">ARP · Lock seed</button><button data-hw="11">REC · Variation</button><button data-hw="2">ENV · Undo</button><button data-hw="3" id="freeze">LFO · Freeze</button><button data-hw="7">SAVE · Store patch</button></div><div class="subcontrols"><label>Tempo <input id="tempo" type="range" min="30" max="220" value="76"></label><output id="bpm">76 BPM</output><label>Master <input id="master" type="range" min="0" max="4096" value="2700"></label><button id="panic">Panic</button></div></div></div><div class="keyboard-head"><span>PLAY THE SELECTED VOICE</span><div><button data-hw="12">OCT −</button> <output id="octave">Octave 0</output> <button data-hw="13">OCT +</button></div></div><div class="keys" id="keys"></div><label class="typing"><input id="typing-keys" type="checkbox"> Play with typing keys: A W S E D R F G Y H U J · F to E · use OCT for other octaves</label><div class="note">Hold a function button to see its controls explained on the display. Tap to use it. EDIT: Sound → Filter → Envelope → Mix. SEQ: Rhythm → Groove. FX: Granular → Tape. GLO: Harmony → System → Look. HOME + PRESET: Biome. EDIT + PRESET: sound preset. Every track can use every engine.</div></section>
-<section class="patch-library"><button id="midi-connect">Connect MIDI input</button><select id="midi-input" aria-label="MIDI input"><option value="">No MIDI input</option></select><label>User name <input id="bank-name" maxlength="23" value="MY BIOME" aria-label="User Biome or sound name"></label><button id="bank-load">Load user slot</button><button id="bank-save">Save user slot</button><p>Begin with Blank or any factory Biome. Shape your six voices and phrases, then use GLO → User Banks to select one of 16 Biome slots or 64 sound slots. Enter a name, stop playback, choose internal clock and save. In browser mode, an occupied slot requires a second Save within three seconds. The live FM-1 editor instead asks you to confirm replacement. Browser banks stay in this browser; hardware banks stay on the FM-1. Export each finished Biome as a file for safekeeping. Granular audio is not stored.</p></section><div id="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><section class="roots" aria-label="Thank you to the community"><div><span class="eyebrow">GROWING THROUGH YOUR FEEDBACK</span><h2>Thank you for listening.</h2></div><div><p>Your response to Mutable Dreams has shaped this next chapter. Your requests for warmer sounds, personal Biomes and dependable performance are at the heart of 1.1. Thank you for making music with it, and for telling us what could be better.</p></div></section><div class="footer-grid"><div><h2>Every voice is yours.</h2><p>Fill all six tracks with percussion, resonant strings, soft chords, or any combination. Choose from 224 sound presets while keeping your notes, rhythm, levels and sends. An empty Biome is a starting point for a world of your own.</p></div><div><h2>Chance, with a memory.</h2><p>Euclidean patterns, swing, accents and repeats meet eight shared scales. Lock a seed with ARP, make a variation with REC, and undo it with ENV. Freeze, reverse or transpose the granular cloud as your rhythm keeps moving.</p></div><div><h2>Room to be clear.</h2><p>Full-rate granular recording, gently overlapping grains and a cleaner signal path bring more detail. Open the filter for clarity or close it for warmth. Gentle resonance and fundamental-led presets keep softer sounds within easy reach. FULL offers richer processing; dense combinations automatically use ECO to protect playback on the FM-1.</p></div></div>
