 <section id="watch" class="watch update-film" aria-labelledby="film-title"><span class="eyebrow">THE 1.1 WALKTHROUGH / SHAPED BY YOUR FEEDBACK</span><h2 id="film-title">Warmer worlds.<br>Your own Biomes.</h2><p>Thank you for the music, thoughtful questions and generous feedback. Take a quiet tour of the new voices, mixer, shared effects, phrases and User Banks, then hear the granular bus on a real FM-1.</p><video controls preload="none" playsinline poster="Mutable-Dreams-1.1-Thumbnail.jpg"><source src="Mutable-Dreams-1.1-Tutorial-Web.mp4" type="video/mp4"><track kind="captions" srclang="en" label="English" src="Mutable-Dreams-1.1-Tutorial.vtt"></video><nav class="chapter-links" aria-label="Video chapters"><button type="button" data-seek="0.000">0:00 · Thank you</button><button type="button" data-seek="33.583">0:33 · Warmer voices</button><button type="button" data-seek="82.083">1:22 · A shared space</button><button type="button" data-seek="119.500">1:59 · Inside the grain</button><button type="button" data-seek="201.833">3:21 · Movement with intention</button><button type="button" data-seek="245.167">4:05 · Your phrase, your Biome</button><button type="button" data-seek="293.417">4:53 · Two worlds, one instrument</button><button type="button" data-seek="339.917">5:39 · Keep your worlds safe</button><button type="button" data-seek="383.833">6:23 · With gratitude</button></nav><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RCgs8t8fXvM">Watch on Kid Bunka / YouTube</a> · <a href="Update-Notes-1.1.txt">Read the 1.1 update notes</a> · <a href="Mutable-Dreams-1.1-Tutorial.srt" download>English captions</a> · <a href="Mutable-Dreams-1.1-Transcript.txt">Transcript</a> · <a href="https://github.com/kidbee85-beep/mutable-dreams/releases/tag/v1.1">Firmware and complete source</a></p><p class="fine">Music recorded directly from an FM-1 running this release. The film shows native Mutable Dreams 1.1 views rendered from the release source; it is not a camera recording of live editing. Calm generated male narration. Selected original Mutable Instruments algorithms retain their credits; this independent project is not endorsed by Mutable Instruments or M-VAVE.</p></section><section id="install" class="install-section"><span class="eyebrow">MUTABLE DREAMS 1.1 / INSTALL &amp; RETURN</span><h2>Keep your worlds safe.</h2><p>Update directly from Mutable Dreams 1.0 or install from the original Stock V15. The test report records the checked routes and exact firmware files. Use the backup procedure for your current version. On 1.1, back up saved banks as .mddb and export unsaved live edits as JSON; 1.0 uses the legacy guide. Returning to V15 erases User Banks and preferences; restore your backup after reinstalling 1.1.</p><div class="install-actions"><a class="primary" href="Mutable-Dreams-1.1-Install.html">Install or return to V15</a><a href="Recovery-1.1.txt">Backup &amp; recovery guide</a><a href="Mutable-Dreams-1.1-Source.zip">Complete source</a><a href="DEVICE-TEST-REPORT.txt">Device test report</a></div><p>The hardware editor shows live parameters; sound comes from the FM-1. Browser mode is a complete independent instrument with its own saved banks. Your downloaded firmware, source, recovery instructions and checksums are available together.</p><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PP6dAPAhIrQ">Watch the original 1.0 tutorial</a> · <a href="https://mutable-dreams.sugarypixie10.chatgpt.site/Mutable-Dreams-1.0.html">Original 1.0 site and recovery instructions</a></p></section><section class="roots" aria-labelledby="roots-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">WITH GRATITUDE / OUR ROOTS</span><h2 id="roots-title">From a generous idea,<br>new worlds can grow.</h2></div><div><p>Mutable Dreams owes its foundations to <strong>Émilie Gillet and Mutable Instruments</strong>. Their instruments and openly shared code made this exploration possible. Selected original algorithms from Plaits, Rings and the new Elements Strike subset form part of our sound engine, with their original credits and MIT notices preserved.</p><p>Our contribution is a six-voice instrument for the FM-1: editable Biomes, generative rhythms, a custom granular bus, and an interface that invites discovery. We want to carry that spirit of curiosity into something approachable, expressive, and unmistakably its own.</p><nav aria-label="Original Mutable Instruments work"><a href="https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack">Explore the original source ↗</a><a href="https://pichenettes.github.io/mutable-instruments-documentation/modules/plaits/">Discover Plaits ↗</a><a href="https://pichenettes.github.io/mutable-instruments-documentation/modules/rings/">Discover Rings ↗</a></nav><p class="credits-note">An independent community project, unaffiliated with and not endorsed by Mutable Instruments. These are selected algorithms, not complete module ports. Our granular bus and Round Bass are our own designs. Marbles-inspired remembered variation, Tides-inspired cyclic modulation and Warps-inspired ring blending are original implementations, not complete ports of those modules.</p></div></section>
 <div class="tiny">Mutable Dreams · Independent firmware for the M-VAVE FM-1. Selected DSP: Émilie Gillet / Mutable Instruments, MIT. Device platform and simulator: fm1-base / felucca-bsp, MPL-2.0. This browser runs the firmware sound engine; FM-1 performance is measured separately. Browser saves stay on this computer. 16 named User Biomes and 64 user sound slots; factory Biomes remain available. Export your finished Biomes as files for safekeeping. Granular memory: 2.97 seconds, mono PCM16 at 44.1 kHz, with stereo grains. ECO uses half-rate FM / VA / Harmonic voices. <a href="DEVICE-TEST-REPORT.txt">Read the measurements and limitations ↗</a></div></main>
